# Failing-first fresh-slot relaunch replays in tests/fm-relaunch-fresh-slot.test.sh: a herdr ship recorded in an older same-origin clone relaunches into a free slot of this home's clone through the ordinary spawn path (new pane, slot claimed, branch at the old copy's HEAD fetched from the copy because origin lacks it, nothing pushed, record naming the live clone and slot, old pane closed and old copy returned with its claim released), both through fm-spawn --relaunch and end to end through fm-control relaunch. Origin's branch is used when it already holds the copy's HEAD; an older live branch moves forward; a live branch outside the copy's history, and a copy off its branch, refuse; uncommitted work (including an edit an ignored submodule hides) refuses in fm-control before the agent is stopped, and a full live pool defers there; a failure after the slot is claimed and before the new record returns the slot and keeps the old copy; two spellings of one origin match. Each fails on 2703782f and passes here; a ship whose home clone has another origin stays where it is on both. A recorded worktree that belongs to another repository refuses in fm-control before the agent stops and in fm-spawn before any import; fails at 23db09ed. An old copy whose slot claim names another task is refused in both places and never returned, and the other task's claim is untouched; fails at 0f99f020.
